        {
          "local_term": "Sous-paragraphe",
          "name": "sous-paragraphe",
          "description": "Rare fourth-level division in some codes, below Sous-section",
          "bluebell_proxy": "SUBSECTION",
          "requires_postprocessing": true
        }
      ],
      "note": "French codes (Code civil, Code penal, Code du travail, etc.) use a distinctive article numbering scheme: L.xxx-x (legislative part), R.xxx-x (regulatory/decret en CE), D.xxx-x (decret simple). Article numbers encode their position in the hierarchy (e.g., L.1234-5 = Livre 1, Titre 2, Chapitre 3, Art. 4 no. 5). Codification performed by DILA. Codes are maintained at legifrance.gouv.fr as consolidated versions."
    }
